# Shell scripts must stay LF on checkout. core.autocrlf is true on this machine,
# and a CRLF shebang line makes the script unrunnable: bash reads the trailing
# \r as part of the interpreter path and reports "bash\r: No such file or
# directory". Scoped to *.sh deliberately - a repo-wide text=auto would
# renormalise every tracked file at once.
*.sh text eol=lf
